    "['pw-template [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'l2vpn xconnect context pwt', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'l2vpn xconnect context pwt', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nl2vpn xconnect context pwt\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei `pw-template pwt` command creates a pseudowire template named \"pwt\" for Layer 2 VPN connections. The equivalent Cisco command is `l2vpn xconnect context pwt`, which establishes a similar pseudowire template context for Layer 2 VPN connections.\\n\\nNote that the Cisco command only creates the context - the peer address and other parameters would need to be configured separately within this context, whereas Huawei\\'s pw-template includes these parameters directly in the template definition.', 'trans_template': 'l2vpn xconnect context pwt'}]]": 1,
    "['peer-address [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'l2vpn xconnect context', 'parent_command': ['l2vpn xconnect context pwt'], 'root': 'l2vpn xconnect context pwt', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nl2vpn xconnect context\\n member pseudowire 3.3.3.9 100\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei `peer-address` command within a PW template specifies the remote PE's LSR ID for the pseudowire. In Cisco, the equivalent is creating an L2VPN XConnect context and specifying the remote peer IP (3.3.3.9) along with the VC ID (100 in this case, taken from the `mpls l2vc` command in the interface configuration). The VC ID must match between both peers.\", 'trans_template': 'l2vpn xconnect context'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'member pseudowire 3.3.3.9 100', 'parent_command': ['l2vpn xconnect context pwt'], 'root': 'l2vpn xconnect context pwt', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nl2vpn xconnect context\\n member pseudowire 3.3.3.9 100\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei `peer-address` command within a PW template specifies the remote PE's LSR ID for the pseudowire. In Cisco, the equivalent is creating an L2VPN XConnect context and specifying the remote peer IP (3.3.3.9) along with the VC ID (100 in this case, taken from the `mpls l2vc` command in the interface configuration). The VC ID must match between both peers.\", 'trans_template': 'member pseudowire 3.3.3.9 100'}]]": 1,
